            <DIV class=3Dsbody>You can surpass the 26 drive letter =
limitation by=20
            using NTFS junction points. By using junction points, you =
can graft=20
            a target folder onto another NTFS folder or "mount" a volume =
onto an=20
            NTFS junction point. Junction points are transparent to =
programs.=20
            <P class=3DtopOfPage><A=20
            href=3D"http://support.microsoft.com/kb/205524#top"><IMG =
alt=3D""=20
            =
src=3D"http://support.microsoft.com/library/images/support/kbgraphics/pub=
lic/en-us/uparrow.gif">Back=20
            to the top</A></P>
            <H3 id=3DtocHeadRef>Preview Tools for NTFS Junction =
Points</H3>
            <SCRIPT type=3Dtext/javascript>loadTOCNode(2, =
'summary');</SCRIPT>
            Microsoft offers three utilities for creating and =
manipulating NTFS=20
            junction points:=20
            <H4 id=3DtocHeadRef>Linkd.exe</H4>
            <SCRIPT type=3Dtext/javascript>loadTOCNode(3, =
'summary');</SCRIPT>

