'moreinformation');</SCRIPT>

            <DIV class=3Dsbody>
            <H3 id=3DtocHeadRef>Sample Usage</H3>
            <SCRIPT=20
            type=3Dtext/javascript>loadTOCNode(2, =
'moreinformation');</SCRIPT>

            <TABLE class=3D"list ul">
              <TBODY>
              <TR>
                <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                <TD class=3Dtext>To create a junction point to your =
desktop:
                  <TABLE class=3D"list ol">
                    <TBODY>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>1.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>At a command prompt, type <SPAN=20
                        class=3DuserInput>linkd mydesktop <VAR><VAR>user =

                        profile</VAR></VAR>\desktop</SPAN> (where =
<VAR><VAR>user=20
                        profile</VAR></VAR> is the name of the user=20
                    profile).</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>2.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>Type <SPAN class=3DuserInput>dir=20
                        mydesktop</SPAN> to display the contents of your =

                      desktop.</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                <TD class=3Dtext>To list the available volumes on your =
system,=20
                  at a command prompt, type <SPAN=20
                  class=3DuserInput>mountvol</SPAN>.<CODE><PRE =
class=3Dcode>\\?\Volume{e2464851-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\ C:\=20

\\?\Volume{e2464852-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\ D:\=20

\\?\Volume{e2464850-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\ R:\=20
					</PRE></CODE><B>NOTE</B>: The string after "Volume" is=20
                  the GUID that is used to identify a unique volume even =
if the=20
                  drive letter changes.<BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                <TD class=3Dtext>To mount your CD-ROM onto an NTFS =
junction=20
                  point:
                  <TABLE class=3D"list ol">
                    <TBODY>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>1.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>At a command prompt, type <SPAN=20
                        class=3DuserInput>md cd</SPAN>.</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>2.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>Type <SPAN =
class=3DuserInput>mountvol cd=20
                        =
\\?\Volume{e2464850-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\</SPAN>.</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>3.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>Type <SPAN class=3DuserInput>dir =
cd</SPAN>=20
                        to display the contents of your=20
                  CD-ROM.</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                <TD class=3Dtext>To mount another volume onto an NTFS =
junction=20
                  point on your system drive:
                  <TABLE class=3D"list ol">
                    <TBODY>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>1.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>At a command prompt, type <SPAN=20
                        class=3DuserInput>md ddrive</SPAN>.</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>2.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>Type <SPAN =
class=3DuserInput>mountvol=20
                        ddrive=20
                        =
\\?\Volume{e2464852-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\</SPAN></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dnumber>3.</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>Type <SPAN class=3DuserInput>dir=20
                        ddrive</SPAN> to displays the contents of drive=20
                    D.</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><B>NOTE</B>: When you =
display the=20
                  contents of a folder by using the "dir" command, NTFS =
junction=20
                  points are indicated by {Junction}.<BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                <TD class=3Dtext>To delete junction points:
                  <TABLE class=3D"list ul">
                    <TBODY>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>To delete the mydesktop junction =
point,=20
                        at a command prompt, type <SPAN =
class=3DuserInput>linkd=20
                        mydesktop /d</SPAN> or <SPAN =
class=3DuserInput>Delrp=20
                        mydesktop</SPAN>.</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>To delete the CD mount point, at =
a=20
                        command prompt, type <SPAN =
class=3DuserInput>mountvol=20
                        =
\\?\Volume{e2464850-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\=20
                        /d</SPAN>.</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD class=3Dbullet>=E2=80=A2</TD>
                      <TD class=3Dtext>To delete the ddrive mount point, =
at a=20
                        command prompt, type <SPAN =
class=3DuserInput>mountvol=20
                        =
\\?\Volume{e2464852-8089-11d2-8803-806d6172696f}\=20
                        =
/d</SPAN>.</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>
